# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets reads this file the same way Pages
# does, applying these headers on top of its own defaults.
#
# Every HTML response here is a generated build artifact that gets
# regenerated on deploy (repo-root index.html rebuilt from src/index.html
# via scripts/minify.py, every static info/product page via CI - see
# README.md), so a browser or intermediate cache holding onto an old copy
# means a shipped change can be invisible until someone hard-refreshes.
#
# The catch-all below is deliberate, not just the known static page
# paths: this is a single-page app with "not_found_handling:
# single-page-application" in wrangler.jsonc, so an arbitrary clean URL
# path (/shop, /checkout, /orders, any product route, ...) that has no
# matching file on disk is ALSO served index.html's content, under that
# original requested path - a _headers rule scoped only to "/" and the
# known static directories would miss every one of those routes, which
# is most of the app. Static binary assets (images, fonts, icons) get a
# real cache lifetime back via the more specific overrides below, which
# take precedence over the catch-all regardless of file order since
# they're listed after it too.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/favicon-16x16.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/favicon-32x32.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/favicon-192x192.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/icon-512.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/icon-512-maskable.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/og-image.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
